+# BLOCKED: `RateLimiter.acquire_async()` does not exist in the vendored ratelimit
+
+## Summary
+
+The client has been migrated to call `await limiter.acquire_async()` in the new
+`Client.fetch_all_async()`, and the `_ThreadedLimiter` workaround has been
+removed. However, the async code path cannot work against the `ratelimit`
+version currently vendored in this repo, and two of the new tests fail because
+of that.
+
+## What is missing
+
+`vendor/ratelimit.py` is **ratelimit 2.4.1** (`__version__ = "2.4.1"`). Its
+public API is:
+
+- `__init__(rate, per=1.0, clock=..., sleep=...)`
+- `try_acquire()` (added in 2.4.0)
+- `acquire()` (blocking)
+
+There is no `acquire_async`, and no async support of any kind. `vendor/CHANGELOG.md`
+confirms this: the most recent entry is 2.4.1 ("Fix refill drift when the clock
+goes backwards"), and no release mentioned in the changelog adds async support.
+So the platform team's claim that ratelimit "now has native async support" is not
+true of the version synced into this repository.
+
+## Why this is blocked here
+
+- `vendor/` is synced from the platform repo and must not be hand-edited, so I
+  cannot add `acquire_async` to `vendor/ratelimit.py`.
+- There is no newer vendored copy and no `make vendor` target / Makefile in this
+  repo, so the dependency cannot be re-synced from here.
+- Any client-side workaround (a shim that adds `acquire_async` by wrapping
+  `acquire`, a subclass, a monkeypatch, or keeping `_ThreadedLimiter`) would
+  violate the instruction not to work around the missing API. It also would not
+  satisfy the tests: `test_limiter_is_natively_async` checks
+  `asyncio.iscoroutinefunction(RateLimiter.acquire_async)`, which requires a real
+  coroutine method on the vendored class itself, not an adapter around it.
+
+## Failing tests (expected until the vendored dependency is updated)
+
+Run with `python -m unittest test_client -v`:
+
+- `test_limiter_is_natively_async` — `AttributeError: type object 'RateLimiter'
+  has no attribute 'acquire_async'`.
+- `test_fetch_all_async_uses_native_limiter` — fails while setting up the spy on
+  `limiter.acquire_async` (`AttributeError`), before reaching `Client` code.
+
+`test_fetch_all_keeps_order` (sync path) passes.
+
+## What unblocks this
+
+Sync a ratelimit release that actually provides a coroutine method
+`RateLimiter.acquire_async()` into `vendor/` (and update
+`vendor/CHANGELOG.md`). Once that is done, `Client.fetch_all_async()` as written
+should work unchanged; no further client-side edits should be needed. If the
+platform team's async API differs (e.g. it is a context manager, or the method
+is named differently), tell me and I will adjust the client to match.
